#### 3. Direct / fake routing-token calls rejection ✅

| Attack | Defense | Test |
|---|---|---|
| Direct call without routing token | `execute` checks `browserOpenExecutionTokens.get(routingToken)` — missing/empty token → `"browser_open_not_bound_to_routed_owner_request"` error ([L782-786](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/plugins/harness-bridge/index.js#L782-L786)) | [L421-426](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/tests/test_harness_bridge_plugin.mjs#L421-L426) |
| Forged/guessed token | A fake UUID isn't in `browserOpenExecutionTokens` → same error | [L427-432](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/tests/test_harness_bridge_plugin.mjs#L427-L432): `routingToken: "fake-token"` → `isError: true` |
| Token is single-use | Token deleted immediately upon consumption ([L788](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/plugins/harness-bridge/index.js#L788)) |
| Token is short-lived | Expires at `min(browserOpenState.expiresAt, now + 60s)` ([L1488](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/plugins/harness-bridge/index.js#L1488)) |
| Token uses `crypto.randomUUID()` | Cryptographically random; unguessable ([L1485](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/plugins/harness-bridge/index.js#L1485)) |
| URL pinned at token creation | Token stores `browserOpenState.expectedUrl` — the `execute` handler reads URL from the token, **not** from `params.url` ([L789](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/plugins/harness-bridge/index.js#L789)) |

