### Additional observations (no safety issues)

- **Map size capping**: All run-tracking maps are capped at 1024 entries with time-based expiry ([L1097-1117](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/plugins/harness-bridge/index.js#L1097-L1117)) — no unbounded memory growth.
- **URL normalization**: `normalizeBrowserUrl` validates protocol is `http:` or `https:`, strips credentials ([L99-103](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/plugins/harness-bridge/index.js#L99-L103)).
- **Plugin manifest**: `harness_browser_open` is declared in `contracts.tools` ([L24](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/plugins/harness-bridge/openclaw.plugin.json#L24)).
- **`browser-open` via shell is not blocked by `isHighImpactBrowserShellCall`** ([L68-73](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/tests/test_harness_bridge_plugin.mjs#L68-L73)) — correctly returns `false` since `browser-open` is the safe read-only command, not a high-impact action. However, during an active browser-open routing run, all shell calls are blocked by the catch-all ([L1498-1504](file:///Users/juntae.park/projects/harness-platform/plugins/harness-bridge/index.js#L1498-L1504)).
